        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Christopher Tin, Jacqueline Horner-Kwiatek\n- Products: Calling All Dawns, Baba Yetu, Civilization IV, The Drop That Contained the Sea\n- Organizations: Anonymous 4, Grammy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- In 2005, the video game Civilization IV used the song \"Baba Yetu\" as its theme.\n- \"Baba Yetu\" is a song by composer Christopher Tin.\n- At the 53rd Grammy Awards, the album Calling All Dawns won Best Classical Crossover Album.\n- At the 53rd Grammy Awards, the song \"Baba Yetu\" won Best Instrumental Arrangement Accompanying Vocalist(s).\n- Jacqueline Horner-Kwiatek is a member of the ensemble Anonymous 4.\n- Jacqueline Horner-Kwiatek was a featured soloist on Christopher Tin's Grammy award-winning CD Calling All Dawns.\n- In 2014, Christopher Tin released The Drop That Contained the Sea as a classical crossover album.",
